          "overview": "## Filesystem MCP Server\n\nThe filesystem-mcp-server is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that gives AI assistants direct, structured access to the local filesystem. It allows AI-driven workflows to read, write, and organize files and directories as part of a larger reasoning process, making persistent storage and file-based context a first-class capability inside MCP-compatible assistants. The server enables use cases including developer workflows, data preparation, note-taking, and artifact generation where AI systems need controlled access to local files."
